     And what effect would it have, aside from potential use
of aligned artifacts?  If you pay attention, you'll notice that
when your character changes alignment all monsters already in
play retain the same peacefulness/hostility demeanor--they don't
all suddenly swap their attitudes.

     As a more practical matter, the only monsters with varying
alignment are minions ("<foo> of <deity>") and temple priests
(who are basically supersets of lesser minions).  While a minion
can be flagged as tame, it will not behave like a regular pet.
There's no way to track hunger or fetching/dropping history;
the internal bookkeeping used for minions is mutally exclusive
with that used for pets.


